events.body:
Thanks both. Yes, I’d like to open the PR for the main change, since I have the measurement setup to back it.

@tanish-malekar on include_output_tokens, as far as I can read on v0.30.0, decode positions are still written with K=0. Each decode step schedules the previously sampled token at its own slot, and propose() writes every scheduled row [extract_hidden_states.py:132-154](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.30.0/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/extract_hidden_states.py#L132). So the drafts may not be needed for it. I’ll include a test comparing saved hidden states with drafts on and off, include_output_tokens included, which should settle whether the default can change.

@ningyuting7-boop, the sync-scheduling fix stands on its own, as you say. Please go ahead with that as a separate PR, and I’ll keep mine to the K=0 behaviour for extract_hidden_states.
